    {
      "id": "claim_9f72c9ba4c254c1b8e9ebe4873844563",
      "statement": "RequestContext construction creates the Flask Request from the WSGI environment and defers routing failures by storing an HTTPException; pushing a request context ensures a same-application AppContext, binds the request ContextVar, opens the session, and then matches the URL so custom converters can access session data.",
